Subject: [PATCH 26/26] Navigation: a route back from every packet, the retired
 signposts out of search, the packets in the map
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three small gaps the packet work exposed.

A reviewer who lands on a packet from an invitation email had the sidebar and
nothing else — no line saying where the terms, the lane table, or the other packets
live. Each builder now writes a one-line route into the packet's header: the
reviewer page for the seat's terms, the packets index one level up. Regenerated,
per the rule.

The nine retired docs/0X signposts existed so old links land; they were also in the
search index, so searching "track record" surfaced the signpost above the page it
points to. They are now search_exclude in _config.yml — reachable by link, invisible
to search, same treatment the archive already had.

MAP.md claims to answer "which file owns this question" for the whole repository and
had no row for packets/. It now has a table: the index owns the packet rule; the
three packets are marked derived and owning nothing, because the sweep, the queue
and the register remain the authority — the map now says out loud what the packets'
own headers say.
